PROBE SOURCE + FINDING F1 (step 3) — worker-d6e44333, 2026-09-06.

=== THE PROBE, FULL SOURCE (global rail 12b: recreatable, deleted after use). Written to %TEMP%\activation-probe-d6e44333.mjs, run with `node <probe> "<store.sqlite>"`, Node v24.16.0. ===

    import { measureActivationReceipts, nodeActivationReceiptPorts } from
      "file:///D:/projexts/moe-next/apps/daemon/src/bootstrap/activation-receipts-measure.js";
    import { activationWitnessOf } from
      "file:///D:/projexts/moe-next/apps/daemon/src/bootstrap/activation-receipts.js";

    const root = "D:/projexts/moe-next";
    const receipts = await measureActivationReceipts({
      agentCommand: "claude",
      artifactRoot: root,
      projectId: "probe-bb844c28",
      projectRoot: root,
      storePath: process.argv[2],
    }, nodeActivationReceiptPorts({
      committedProbeRef: () => Promise.resolve("probe/committed-provider-probe-ref"),
      installedPolicySliceRefs: () => Promise.resolve(["policy/slice-a", "policy/slice-b"]),
    }));

    for (const m of receipts.members) {
      console.log(`${m.member.padEnd(13)} measured=${m.measured} ` +
        (m.measured ? `ref=${m.ref} hash=${m.hash ?? "-"} detail=${m.detail}`
                    : `code=${m.code} layer=${m.layer} detail=${m.detail}`));
    }
    console.log("signing      ", JSON.stringify(receipts.signing));
    console.log("repository   ", JSON.stringify(receipts.repository));
    console.log("store        ", JSON.stringify(receipts.store));
    console.log("distribution ", JSON.stringify(receipts.distribution));
    const w = activationWitnessOf(receipts);
    console.log("WITNESS ok=", w.ok);
    console.log(JSON.stringify(w.ok ? w.witness : w.refusals, null, 2));

The two overrides stand in for the daemon's durable readers (activation-command-entry.ts:37-48 wires exactly these two against the real store). WITHOUT them the production default is `null`/`[]` and activation refuses ACTIVATION_PROVIDER_UNMEASURED / ACTIVATION_POLICY_UNMEASURED — the fail-closed behaviour, reproduced live on the first run of this probe, which also refused store+backup against a path that had been pruned out from under it.

STORE ARG used for the green run: a real 225280-byte moe SQLite store copied out of tree. Backup written by the run: `.moe-next/backups/20260906020626290.sqlite`, sha256 `afede285f646a01b2782e66131ca9281f321386bbf1fb22b6b774a983e61c101`, re-computed by me and byte-identical to the source. `.moe-next/` is gitignored (.gitignore:76) and `BACKUP_RETENTION = 5` prunes, so repeated activations do not accumulate or dirty the tree — verified: exactly 5 files present throughout.

=== FINDING F1 — the browser's chain still sends TWO invented caller observations. NOT chargeable to any child (all five DONE+approved); recorded here per the DELIVERY-BIAS rail as a follow-up, not a new row. ===

The daemon-minted WITNESS is honest — that is what this epic's row set fixed and it holds. But the two chain steps that carry a CALLER half still ship fixture literals, and the card reads them from `DEV_PAYLOADS` (`activation-port.ts:70` -> `apps/control-room/src/live/live-dispatch-payloads.ts`):

1. `provider.probe` (:118-149) registers a profile asserting a version reading nobody took:
     modelSnapshotKind:     "DATED_SNAPSHOT"
     modelSnapshotEvidence: "claude --version reported a dated snapshot"
     capabilitySchemaDigest: hex64("ca9ab111")
     truthClass:            "DAEMON_VERIFIED"
   The demo seed deliberately refuses to do this: `demo-seed-policy.ts:106` uses `modelSnapshotKind: "UNKNOWN"` with the comment "refuses to assert a `claude --version` the demo never took". So on this one axis the browser card is now LESS honest than the seed it replaced. This is why DoD 2's literal "provider CLI version" is unmet: `grep -rn '\-\-version' apps/daemon/src --include=*.ts` shows no version probe anywhere on the activation path.

2. `project.bind_repository` (:120-126) sends `baseRevisionHash: hex64("beef")`, `repositoryRef: "repo-1"`, `truthClass: "DAEMON_VERIFIED"` — while the MEASURED equivalent already exists and is exported: `repositoryObservationOf` (`activation-receipts.ts:205`, derives the observation from the measured repository receipt). `git grep repositoryObservationOf -- apps/` returns only tests, the index barrel and one comment: ZERO production callers.

SUGGESTED CLOSE (one row, daemon-side, mirrors what child B did for `project.activate`): make `project.bind_repository` and `provider.probe` daemon-measured too — bind from `repositoryObservationOf`, probe from a real `claude --version` / `codex --version` with `modelSnapshotKind: "UNKNOWN"` when it cannot be read — and refuse a caller-supplied observation the same way `ACTIVATION_WITNESS_CALLER_SUPPLIED` refuses a caller witness.
